              "type": "text",
              "text": "Warragamba Dam is filled by runoff from a catchment area of 9050 square kilometres.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In a storm, 40 mm of rain fell. What is the increase in the volume of the dam?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$362\\,000\\,000\\text{ m}^3$",
      "worked": "Assuming all rainfall over the catchment reaches the dam:\n$$\\begin{align*} A &= 9050\\times1\\,000\\,000\\text{ m}^2 \\\\ A &= 9\\,050\\,000\\,000\\text{ m}^2 \\\\ h &= 40\\div1000\\text{ m} \\\\ h &= 0.04\\text{ m} \\\\ V &= Ah \\\\ V &= 9\\,050\\,000\\,000\\times0.04\\text{ m}^3 \\\\ V &= 362\\,000\\,000\\text{ m}^3 \\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
